---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How often should solar panels be cleaned in coastal NSW?',
    answer:
      'For properties within 2km of the coast across Sydney, the Central Coast, and Newcastle, we recommend a clean every six months. Airborne salt spray builds up a fine film that steadily dulls output. For properties further inland, an annual optimization schedule is sufficient unless the array sits directly under heavy tree canopies, bird flight paths, or industrial soot corridors. Rather than relying on a calendar, monitor your inverter app; if your daily peak generation has dropped by 10% or more on a clear day compared to last season, it’s worth booking a clean.',
    open: true,
  },
  {
    question: 'Why is robotic solar panel cleaning safer than traditional manual cleaning?',
    answer:
      'Manual cleaning often means someone working on the roof with long poles and squeegees, which brings fall risk and can crack fragile roof tiles. Salt Spray Solar uses lightweight robotic crawlers instead. Weighing under 7kg, they spread their weight across the array on soft rubber tracks and apply even, gentle pressure, so no one has to walk across your panels to clean them.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can high-pressure washing be used to clean solar panels?',
    answer:
      'Absolutely not. Utilizing a high-pressure washer on solar infrastructure is a critical mistake, and many panel manufacturers say it will void the warranty. The intense pressure easily forces water past the factory rubber seals and straight into the sub-surface laminates, junction boxes, or internal wiring. This can cause hidden moisture damage that shows up as electrical faults months later. Abrasive household brooms and harsh chemical detergents can also wear away the anti-reflective glass coating engineered to maximize light absorption. We use exclusively soft, spinning nylon brushes and pure water.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why does the water quality matter for solar optimization?',
    answer:
      'Standard household tap water is full of dissolved minerals like calcium, magnesium, and iron. When sprayed onto hot solar glass under the Australian sun, the water evaporates instantly, leaving behind a cloudy, hard mineral scale. This white residue blocks sunlight and can help dust stick to the glass. Salt Spray Solar utilizes a heavy-duty, 4-stage Reverse Osmosis and Deionization (RO/DI) filtration trolley on-site. It removes virtually all dissolved minerals from the water, so it dries spot-free.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is a thermal imaging drone solar inspection, and do I need one?',
    answer:
      'Solar cell degradation and internal hardware faults happen silently beneath the glass and are completely invisible to the naked eye. Our premium aerial thermal imaging drone audits use infrared sensors to map the exact heat signatures of your system. When a cell is cracked or damaged, or a bypass diode fails, that part of the panel usually runs hotter than the rest, which shows up clearly on an infrared scan. We run these sweeps prior to cleaning to provide commercial facilities and residential clients with a clear digital health report, helping you catch faults early, before they get worse.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Doesn’t standard rain clean my solar panels for free?',
    answer:
      'Only partially, and only on exceptionally steep roofs. On standard residential pitches or flat commercial warehouse roof lines, rain simply sheets across the glass, collects airborne dirt, and pools at the bottom edge frame. As it dries, it leaves behind a thick, opaque “grime band” directly over the bottom row of cells. Rain does little to shift baked-on bird droppings, tree sap, lichen, or sticky maritime salt films. In fact, rain frequently spreads coastal salt films evenly across the glass rather than lifting them off.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Will your cleaning process affect my manufacturer warranty?',
    answer:
      'We clean to your panel manufacturer’s published cleaning instructions: no high-pressure water, no harsh chemicals, and soft brushes with pure water only. Warranty terms vary by brand, so we check the cleaning guidance for your panels before we start. Every robotic clean and thermal drone audit is digitally logged, giving you a dated maintenance record to keep with your system documents.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to be home on the day of the service?',
    answer:
      'No, you do not need to alter your schedule. As long as our technical operator has clear, safe outdoor access to your property’s ground-level garden tap and a clear line of sight to the roof, we can complete the entire job independently. Once our robotic crawler and thermal drone sweeps are complete, we pack up, drain our buffer tank, and email your comprehensive digital efficiency and health report straight to your inbox.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is your pricing structure for a robotic optimization clean?',
    answer:
      'Because every roof line across the NSW corridor has a different panel configuration and height access profile, we keep pricing simple and transparent. Residential services feature a baseline call-out fee of $150 to $180 AUD which includes travel and your first 12 panels. Additional panels scale out at an affordable $8.00 to $15.00 AUD per panel. Commercial and industrial arrays are quoted on a custom sliding scale based on total volume and site compliance logistics. Call, email or use our booking page to get a fixed price for your system.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ — Salt Spray Solar"
  description="Answers on robotic solar panel cleaning, thermal drone inspections, pricing and caring for your panels."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="FAQ"
    title="Clear Answers on"
    emphasis="High-Yield Solar Optimization"
    sub="Everything you need to know about professional robotic panel cleaning, infrared aerial diagnostics, and caring for your panels across Sydney, the Central Coast, and Newcastle."
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions"><Button href={site.bookHref} variant="primary">Get Your Price &amp; Book</Button></Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <Section>
    <FaqList items={faqs} schema class="mt-0" />
  </Section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Still Have Questions About Recovering Your Lost Solar Output?"
    lede="Speak directly with the specialist technician who will be operating the machinery on your roof. Clear answers and careful, high-tech work."
    cards={[
      { label: 'Ready to Lock in Your Date?', tone: 'amber', href: site.bookHref, text: 'Get Your Price & Book' },
      { label: 'Need a Direct Call?', tone: 'teal', contact: true },
    ]}
  />
</BaseLayout>
